& [FindingOne]
  + the initial SHA256 rendering attempted to apply an uppercase-hex formatter directly to a byte array
  + Rust correctly rejected that unsupported formatting operation at compile time
  + correction uses an explicit bounded byte-wise uppercase hexadecimal encoder with no dependency or digest-domain change

& [FindingTwo]
  + one overlong-path refusal produced the correct rejection but was initially classified as Parse rather than Resource
  + the implementation and focused assertion were corrected to retain the closed first-fault taxonomy required by SDA-015
  + the correction changes classification only and does not widen an accepted path status mode command or physical effect

& [FindingThree]
  + explicit staging surfaced Git's warning that a generated controlled-evidence JSON could normalize from CRLF to LF in the committed object
  + the focused runner now normalizes ConvertTo-Json output to LF before writing and the evidence builder normalizes both production and verification serialization
  + focused replay builder self-verification recursive evidence and raw staged-blob comparison are required after the correction

& [Verification]
  + focused debug overflow-checked release static CLI and controlled disposable-repository tests pass after both corrections
  + no unsafe code Cargo dependency provider network hook staging commit push or self-signature authority was introduced

& [Frontier]
  + exact workspace gates evidence closure attribution and publication remain required before completion
